# PowerShell on Windows (auto-trade)

Cursor/agent shell on this machine **must** use PowerShell 7 (`pwsh`), not Windows PowerShell 5.

## Do

- Prefer `pwsh -NoProfile -File path\to\script.ps1` or `python path\to\script.py`.
- Put remote Python/shell bodies in a **local file**, then pipe with:  
  `Get-Content -Raw .\script.py | ssh host "cat > /tmp/x.py && python3 /tmp/x.py"`
- Binary/tar sync: write local `.tgz`, then base64-pipe into a remote **file** extractor (see `deploy/nas/sync-files.ps1`).
- Use single-quoted PowerShell strings for remote command literals when needed:  
  `ssh host 'python3 /tmp/x.py'`

## Don't

- Don't nest `python -c "..."` / `ssh "..."` / regex paren escapes inside one PowerShell double-quoted line.
- Don't use `&&` assuming bash — in pwsh use `;` or separate calls (pwsh 7 supports `&&`, PS5 does not).
- Don't invent inline heredocs for commit/`ssh` that re-enter PowerShell 5 parsing.

## Helpers

- NAS file sync: `pwsh -NoProfile -File deploy/nas/sync-files.ps1 -Files web/static/index.html,...`
- Remote run script: `pwsh -NoProfile -File deploy/nas/run-remote.ps1 -ScriptPath .\tmp_job.py`
